<!--
  The 40x40 circular header control.

  One file, `<include>`d by the three headers that carry it, so HOME, ABOUT US
  and the empty COLLECTION cannot drift apart: the Figma nodes 2393:1665,
  2413:58 and 2429:352 are one component and this is one layout.

  ## What it opens, and why that changed at G1

  It opened `profile-guest` from G-A3 until G1; it now opens `settings`, and the
  profile is reached from `Settings > Аккаунт > Профиль`.

  That is the frozen design's own structure rather than a rearrangement of it.
  The `settings` frame 2517:2758 / 2517:3725 draws Профиль as its **first row**,
  with a value and a chevron - so Settings is the parent surface and the profile
  is a destination inside it. Nothing in the FINAL file shows how `settings`
  itself is reached, and there is no second control available to reach it with:
  both HOME and ABOUT US carry a *second* 40x40 node at the same x=334,y=12
  (2393:1670, 2413:61) which is `visible: false` - authored and switched off, and
  overlapping this one exactly, so the two could never both be drawn.

  One control, therefore, pointing at the parent. Geometry, artwork plate,
  position and hosts are all unchanged; only the glyph and the destination moved.

  ## Geometry

  From the FINAL Figma file: a 40x40 circle at x=334,y=12 inside the 390x64
  band. 390-334-40 = 16, which is the trailing padding those headers already
  have, so this is simply the last child of the header row rather than a
  positioned view - and that is why nothing below the band moves when it lands.
  The 16x16 glyph sits at x=12,y=12 inside the circle - and that inset lives in
  the artwork's own 40x40 viewport rather than as view padding, so the drawable is
  the Figma node at 1:1.

  Not carried by the populated COLLECTION, which keeps its three-dot overflow
  (2399:31129 / 2444:18376), nor by PLAYER.
-->
<!--
  Wrapped in <layout> so data binding generates ViewSettingsEntryBinding and the
  three headers reach it as `binding.settingsEntry.root`. A plain include of a
  non-binding layout gets no generated field at all, which is the compile error
  this shape avoids.
-->
<layout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <ImageView
        android:id="@+id/settings_entry_icon"
        android:layout_width="@dimen/settings_entry_size"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/settings_entry_size"
        android:background="@drawable/bg_settings_entry"
        android:contentDescription="@string/settings_entry_description"
        android:scaleType="fitCenter"
        android:src="@drawable/ic_settings_entry" />
</layout>
